          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "From a bag of 8 green toys, 7 blue toys and 5 red toys, a toy is taken out and placed back into the bag three times in total. Find the probability of the following.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p24-q14-a-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A green toy was taken out first, a blue toy was taken out second and a red toy was taken out last.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{7}{200}$",
          "worked": "Replacement keeps the probabilities unchanged at each draw.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(GBR)&=\\frac{8}{20}\\times\\frac{7}{20}\\times\\frac{5}{20}\\\\P(GBR)&=\\frac{7}{200}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p24-q14-b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "At least one blue toy was taken out.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p24-q14-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{5803}{8000}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p24-q14-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Subtract the probability of no blue toys from 1.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "There are $8+5=13$ non-blue toys. Use the complementary event of drawing no blue toys.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{at least one blue})&=1-\\left(\\frac{13}{20}\\right)^3\\\\P(\\text{at least one blue})&=\\frac{5803}{8000}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p24-q14-c-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A green toy, blue toy and red toy were taken out but not necessarily in that order.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p24-q14-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{21}{100}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p24-q14-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Multiply the probability of one specified order by the six possible orders.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The orders $GBR$, $GRB$, $BGR$, $BRG$, $RGB$ and $RBG$ have equal probabilities.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{one of each colour})&=6\\times\\frac{8}{20}\\times\\frac{7}{20}\\times\\frac{5}{20}\\\\P(\\text{one of each colour})&=\\frac{21}{100}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
